## Problem

# b00t datums have implicit types (`b00t.type = "agent"|"role"|"prd"|"okr"`) but:
# - No formal ontological grounding → types are strings, not logic constants
# - No cross-repo type-safe discovery → a `GuardManagerAgent` in b00t cannot link to
#   equivalent concepts in l3dg3rr or a future physics simulator
# - No invariant enforcement → any agent can write `type = "anything"`
# - No SPARQL/SHACL query path → can't ask "all Dispositions with bouncer enabled"

# Foundation for future: when physics simulator hits b00t, we need invariant
# type-driven discovery across repos/languages. BFO/UFO provides those anchors.

## Finished State

# Every tomllm datum optionally carries:
# ```toml
# [b00t.sysml]
# stereotype = "«Block»"           # SysMLv2 KerML stereotype
# metaclass = "Class"              # KerML metaclass
# bfo_class = "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"  # Role (BFO IRI)
# ufo_kind = "Role"                # UFO ontological kind
# owl_class = "https://b00t.promptexecution.com/ontology#GuardManagerAgent"
# shacl_shape = "GuardManagerShape"  # SHACL shape name in b00t-ontology.ttl

# [b00t.clif]
# CLIF axioms expressed as TOML strings; transpiled to OWL2 at build time
# 🤓 No Rust CLIF parser exists; CLIF is the authoring format, OWL2 is runtime
# axioms = [
#   "(forall (x) (if (GuardManagerAgent x) (Executive-Authorized x)))",
#   "(forall (x) (if (GuardManagerAgent x) (has-audit-log x)))",
# ]
# ```

# `b00t datums graph --format=owl2` → emits `b00t-ontology.ttl` (OWL2/Turtle)
# `b00t datums graph --format=shacl` → emits `b00t-shapes.ttl` (SHACL shapes)
# Both files loadable into Oxigraph or any OWL2 triplestore for SPARQL queries.

## Rust SBOM (research-confirmed, minimal)

# ```toml
# Add to b00t-cli/Cargo.toml [dependencies]
# horned-owl = "1.4"    # OWL2 AST + RDF/XML parser (primary)
# oxrdf = "0.3"         # Lightweight RDF N-Triples/Turtle emitter
# shacl = "0.3"         # SHACL Core validation
# petgraph already in irontology-mcp v0.6 → upgrade to 0.8
# ```

# Note: `oxigraph` (SPARQL) deferred — heavy dep; use oxrdf + petgraph for graph queries first.

## BFO/UFO and SysMLv2 Type Mapping

# 🔗参 `SYSMLV2-KERML-SUPPLEMENT.tomllmd` — canonical vocabulary; do not duplicate here.

## CLIF → OWL2 Transpilation Strategy

# CLIF is the HUMAN authoring format (expressive, readable axioms).
# OWL2/Turtle is the MACHINE runtime format (SHACL validation, SPARQL queries).

# ```
# [b00t.clif].axioms[]  →  offline transpiler  →  b00t-ontology.ttl
#                                                     ↓
#                                                horned-owl parse
#                                                     ↓
#                                                SHACL validate datums
#                                                     ↓
#                                                oxrdf emit Turtle
# ```

# Transpiler: shell script using existing CLIF tools (Common Logic tools, IKRIS project)
# or hand-mapped for the small initial axiom set (< 50 axioms).

## Postel/CLIF Equivalence Classes

# Operator note: "Postel is itself a type of CLIF translation variant."
# CLIF equivalence axioms express input normalization:

# ```clif
# ; All forms of P1/critical/1 are equivalent
# (= (normalize-priority "P1") (normalize-priority "1")
#    (normalize-priority "critical") "P1")
# (= (normalize-priority "P2") (normalize-priority "2")
#    (normalize-priority "high") "P2")
# ```

# These axioms map directly to Rust `value_parser` normalization logic.
# The CLIF axiom is the specification; the Rust parser is the implementation.

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `[b00t.sysml]` section parsed by `tomllm` crate without error
# - [ ] `[b00t.clif]` axioms section stored as string array
# - [ ] `b00t datums graph --format=owl2` emits valid `b00t-ontology.ttl`
# - [ ] `b00t datums graph --format=shacl` emits valid SHACL shapes file
# - [ ] At least 5 datum types have BFO IRI mappings
# - [ ] `horned-owl` can round-trip the emitted OWL2 (parse → serialize)
# - [ ] guard-manager.agent.tomllmd has valid `[b00t.sysml]` section (dogfood)

